# `make ui` copies ui/dist/* into this directory so go:embed can compile it into
# kelson-server (see ../webui.go). That output is a build artifact — the same
# artifact ui/dist holds, which the repository root ignores for the same reason
# — so everything here is ignored except the two files that are genuinely
# source: this file, and the placeholder the binary serves when nobody ran the
# build.
#
# Ignoring the copy rather than committing it is what keeps `git status` clean
# after `make ui`, and it is why the placeholder is not named index.html: a
# tracked index.html would be overwritten by every UI build and show up as a
# modification waiting to be committed by accident.
*
!.gitignore
!placeholder.html
